Fastener Design Manual — NASA-RP-1228 (@mech-fastener-nasa: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mech-sources) { r_78PXGW34SMJ44D965DX01WGZH5
Richard T. Barrett. NASA Reference Publication 1228, March 1990. [Official record](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19900009424) · [Complete 100-page PDF](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19900009424/downloads/19900009424.pdf).

Read the whole manual during the joints study, following materials, coatings, lubrication, corrosion, locking, threads, fatigue, torque, joint loads, rivets and lockbolts into their original assumptions. It supplies useful mechanics and historical design practice, not universal current equipment specifications.

The official record, cover, contents and introduction were inspected on 30 October 2026. The PDF includes a June 2008 erratum concerning coating outgassing. NASA identifies the work as a US-government work with public use permitted; preserve attribution and component notices. Check modern applicable standards, material evidence and actual service conditions separately. A historical table does not establish a safe operating load or tightening procedure for an unidentified joint.

